## Why This Is Asked
This question tests proficiency with partition dynamic programming where subarrays must be non-overlapping and values derive from range statistics. The solution requires careful separation of concerns: precomputing range queries, implementing the DP transition, and reconstructing the solution through pointer tracking.

## Key Concepts
- Non-overlapping contiguous subarrays as partition elements
- Dynamic programming with two-dimensional state tracking
- Range minima preprocessing for O(1) query access
- Solution reconstruction through backpointers
- Complexity optimization through careful algorithm design

## Code Example
```javascript
function maxKSubarraysMin(A, k) {
  const n = A.length;

  // Precompute range minima
  const mins = Array.from({length: n}, () => Array(n).fill(0));
  for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) {
    let m = Infinity;
    for (let j = i; j < n; j++) {
      m = Math.min(m, A[j]);
      mins[i][j] = m;
    }
  }
```

## Why This Is Asked
New angle: exactly k non-overlapping subarrays maximize sum, a knapsack-like DP variant with efficient inner maximization. It mirrors budgeted promotion planning.

## Key Concepts
- DP state: dp[i][t] is the best total for first i elements using t blocks
- Prefix sums P enable O(1) subarray sums
- Optimize inner max with best = max(dp[j-1][t-1]-P[j-1]) up to i
- Reconstruction via pointers to endpoints

## Code Example
```javascript
function maxKSubarrays(a,k){
  const n=a.length;
  const P=[0];
  for(let v of a) P.push(P[P.length-1]+v);
  const dp=Array.from({length:n+1},()=>Array(k+1).fill(-Infinity));
  dp[0].fill(0);
  for(let t=1;t<=k;t++){
    let best=-Infinity;
    for(let i=1;i<=n;i++){
      dp[i][t]=dp[i-1][t];
      best=Math.max(best, dp[i-1][t-1]-P[i-1]);
      const cand=P[i]+best;
      if(cand>dp[i][t]) dp[i][t]=cand;
    }
  }
  return dp[n][k];
}
```

